## Restore counterpart to backup-hcp-cluster-csi.yaml.j2. Rendered by
## restore_hosted_cluster.yaml when oadp_backup_method=csi.
##
## The Restore CR itself is provider- and method-agnostic: restorePVs
## true is what drives the recovery either way. What changes is what
## Velero does underneath - for a data-mover backup it creates a
## DataDownload per volume, provisions a fresh PVC from the CSI
## StorageClass and streams the snapshot data back from S3 into it,
## rather than replaying files from a Kopia repository.
##
## Watch `oc get datadownloads -n openshift-adp` while this runs; the
## Restore stays in "WaitingForPluginOperations" until they complete.
##
## As with the fs variant, the control-plane namespace must be free of
## the objects being restored (HostedCluster, NodePools and their PVCs
## deleted) - existingResourcePolicy: update cannot rewrite immutable
## fields on a live object. Do not delete the InfraEnv: the reprovisioned
## nodes need it to fetch the discovery ISO.
apiVersion: velero.io/v1
kind: Restore
metadata:
  name: "{{ oadp_restore_name }}"
  namespace: openshift-adp
spec:
  backupName: "{{ oadp_backup_name }}"
  restorePVs: true
  existingResourcePolicy: update
  excludedResources:
    - nodes
    - events
    - events.events.k8s.io
    - backups.velero.io
    - restores.velero.io
    - resticrepositories.velero.io
